Z||000000||Standard||07-10-2000||08:57 PM||||that such a little thing could make a big difference.. <BR>I just replaced the pickup coil in the GT, and <B>wow</B>!!  It runs like a whole new car!  Smoothed the idle out, and it feels like I've gained 30 horsepower!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">   And, my car even runs quieter at idle now!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The only thing that didn't go right is that my car still leaks oil after I replaced the dist. O-ring.. grrr  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Also finally got around to hooking up a manual fan switch.. First try the radiator fan wouldn't turn on, but the trunk fan would.. narrowed it down to a bad fan relay in front.  Jury-rigged it with some help from my dad so it'll work for a little while longer.. now I can keep my car cool in traffic! woohoo!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>Fired up the 84 for the first time in a while today, too.  Drove it around to get out the cobwebs... man, i can't believe how much that car makes me smile... <P>Well, that was my day.  Hope yours was as good  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||GT Bastard||07-10-2000||09:19 PM||||Cool... how did you know that it was the ignition pickup coil?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||07-10-2000||11:07 PM||||I had the distributor and pickup coil replace on my 87 last winter.  After 12+ years the original was looking pretty sad inside.  It made a big difference in how the car ran.  I can't remember what I paid to Associated Auto for the remanufactured distributor, but it was well worth the $$..  I can get 30+mpg with the 2.8 in my GT.<P>I don't know what it does in the quarter mile, but it runs nice at 100+.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Standard||07-11-2000||04:34 AM||||I didn't know that it was the pickup coil.. But it was only 8 bucks and I had the dist. out anyways, so I figured what the heck..  the old one pretty much fell apart when I got it out.<P>I also have some acceleration in 5th gear now!  woohoo!  I like this car even more now...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
